---
import ToolPage from '../layouts/ToolPage.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

const title = 'Resume Builder - Free Online Resume Maker, No Signup';
const description =
  'Build a professional resume in your browser and download it as a PDF for free. No signup, no pay-to-download trap, no watermark. Three recruiter-ready templates, live preview, autosave.';
const h1 = 'Free resume builder';
const lede =
  'Write your resume, pick a template, and download the PDF. Free forever, no account, no watermark. Everything stays in your browser.';
---
<ToolPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  h1={h1}
  lede={lede}
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Resume builder', href: '/resume-builder' }]}
  toolName="TruePDF Resume Builder"
  intro={[
    'Most "free" resume builders run the same play: they let you build for free, then hold the finished resume hostage at the download button. An hour of careful writing ends at a paywall, a trial that quietly converts to a subscription, or a watermark stamped across the page unless you pay. The building is free because the building is not the product. Your finished resume is the product, and that is exactly what they charge for. Call it the pay-to-download trap.',
    'This builder is structured so the trap is impossible. There is no server, no account system, and no billing page to bolt a paywall onto. Your words are saved in your own browser, and the PDF download is just your browser printing the page to a file, something no website can charge you for or take away. The resume on your screen and the PDF you send to employers are the same document, and there is no step where a price appears.',
    'You get three readable, single-column templates designed around standard resume headings: Classic uses a traditional serif style, Modern uses a clean sans-serif style, and Compact uses tighter spacing without forcing the resume onto one page. Every section is editable, sections can be shown, hidden, and reordered, entries can be added, removed, and reordered, and the live preview keeps the same content and reading order as the downloaded PDF.',
  ]}
  steps={[
    'Pick a template above the editor: Classic, Modern, or Compact. You can switch at any time without losing anything you typed.',
    'Fill in your contact details and professional summary. Add work experience entries with the "Add position" button, one bullet per line, most recent job first.',
    'Add your education, then group your skills so they scan quickly. Projects, certifications, languages, awards, publications, volunteer work, and courses are optional and can be left empty or hidden with the Show toggle.',
    'Reorder entries with the up and down arrows until the story reads the way you want. Remove anything that does not earn its space.',
    'Check the live preview beside the editor (or the Preview tab on a phone). What you see is what the PDF will contain.',
    'Click "Download PDF". The PDF downloads directly to your device with clickable links for email, website, LinkedIn, and project demos. That is the whole transaction: there is no checkout, because there is nothing to buy.',
  ]}
  specs={[
    ['Cost', 'Free, no limits, no trial'],
    ['Signup', 'None. No account, no email.'],
    ['Watermark', 'None. The PDF is your resume, nothing added.'],
    ['Where your resume is stored', 'In this browser only (local storage). Nothing is uploaded.'],
    ['PDF export', 'Direct PDF download with clickable links.'],
    ['Templates', 'Classic (serif), Modern (sans serif), Compact (tighter spacing); all use one column and standard headings'],
    ['Sections', 'Contact, summary, experience, education, skills, projects, certifications, languages, awards, publications, volunteer, courses. Sections can be toggled on/off and reordered.'],
    ['ATS note', 'Classic uses standard single-column formatting. No template guarantees ATS parsing.'],
    ['Works offline', 'Yes, once the page has loaded'],
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: 'Is this resume builder really free?',
      a: 'Yes, completely. There is no trial, no premium tier, and no credit card step. The reason is structural: the tool runs entirely in your browser and the PDF comes from your browser\u2019s own print function, so there is no server cost to recover and nothing to gate behind a payment. Free here means free, not "free until the download button."',
    },
    {
      q: 'How does the free PDF download work?',
      a: 'Clicking "Download PDF" generates a clean PDF directly in your browser and downloads it — no print dialog. Email, website, LinkedIn, and project demo links are clickable in the PDF.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Where is my resume saved? Is it private?',
      a: 'Your resume is saved automatically to your browser\u2019s local storage on your own device, and it is stated right in the editor: saved in this browser only. It is never uploaded to a server, because there is no server involved. The tradeoff is that clearing your browser data erases it, so keep the downloaded PDF as your permanent copy.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Which template is best for applicant tracking systems (ATS)?',
      a: 'All three templates use a single column, standard section headings, and no graphics or text boxes. These choices are generally easier for parsers to read, but no template can guarantee perfect ATS parsing because systems differ. Choose the visual style you prefer and review the exported PDF before applying.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What is the pay-to-download trap?',
      a: 'It is the business model behind most online resume builders: the editor is free, but downloading your finished resume requires payment, a trial signup, or a subscription. The trap works because it strikes after you have invested an hour of writing, when walking away feels expensive. This builder cannot do that to you because the download is your browser\u2019s print function, not a server feature anyone can lock.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Can I build my resume on my phone?',
      a: 'Yes. On narrow screens the editor and preview become tabs, so you type in the Edit tab and check the result in the Preview tab. The PDF download works from mobile browsers too: use the share or print option and choose "Save as PDF." For long writing sessions a desktop is more comfortable, but nothing about the tool requires one.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What happens if I clear my browser data or switch devices?',
      a: 'Clearing site data wipes the saved resume, and it does not follow you to another device, because it lives only in the browser where you typed it. Treat the downloaded PDF as the real copy: download it whenever you make meaningful changes. If you need the same draft on two devices, download the PDF on one and retype or paste on the other.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Can I import my existing resume instead of retyping it?',
      a: 'Yes. Drop a PDF or Word file on the upload box at the top of the builder and it reads the contact details, experience, education, skills, and projects in your browser. Correct the extracted fields in the review before importing. Scanned PDFs use on-device text recognition, and the optional larger reader runs in your browser too; your resume is never sent to a server.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Do I need an account to use this?',
      a: 'No, and there is no way to create one. Accounts exist so a service can store your data and charge you later; since your resume never leaves your browser, there is nothing an account would do. Open the page, write, download the PDF, close the tab.',
    },
  ]}
>
  <section class="tool-card resume-app" slot="tool" aria-label="Resume builder">
    <div id="rb-import-panel" class="no-print">
      <p class="mono-label">Starting point</p>
      <div id="rb-import-drop" class="dropzone" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Upload an existing resume as a PDF or Word file">
        <div class="dz-icon"><Icon name="upload" size={30} /></div>
        <div class="dz-title">Upload an existing resume</div>
        <div class="dz-sub">Drop a PDF or Word file here, or click to browse. Scanned PDFs are read on this device too.</div>
      </div>
      <input type="file" id="rb-import-file" accept=".pdf,.docx,application/pdf,application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document" hidden />
      <p id="rb-import-status" role="status" hidden></p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <button id="rb-start-blank" class="btn btn-secondary" type="button">Start from a blank resume</button>
        <span class="stamp">Your files never leave your device</span>
      </div>
      <details class="rb-ai-details">
        <summary>Smarter reading (optional)</summary>
        <p class="hint">The standard reader works on this device and is the default. For harder-to-read layouts, you can optionally download a larger model to run on this device:</p>
        <div class="field checkline">
          <input type="radio" name="rb-parse-mode" id="rb-mode-local" value="local" />
          <label for="rb-mode-local">Download and use the on-device model</label>
        </div>
        <p class="hint">This downloads about 430 MB the first time you choose it. It then runs offline and keeps your resume on this device.</p>
        <div class="field checkline">
          <input type="radio" name="rb-parse-mode" id="rb-mode-heuristic" value="heuristic" />
          <label for="rb-mode-heuristic">Standard reader (no AI model)</label>
        </div>
      </details>
      <div id="rb-import-review" hidden>
        <p class="mono-label">Check what was found</p>
        <p>Your file was read on this device. Correct any fields below before importing, or discard and start blank.</p>
        <div class="rb-import-review-grid">
          <img id="rb-import-preview" class="rb-import-preview" alt="First page of the uploaded resume" hidden />
          <div id="rb-import-fields"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <button id="rb-import-use" class="btn" type="button">Use these details</button>
          <button id="rb-import-discard" class="btn btn-secondary" type="button">Discard and start blank</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="resume-toolbar no-print">
      <div class="rb-templates" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Choose a template">
        <label class="rb-template">
          <input type="radio" name="rb-template" value="classic" checked />
          <span>
            <strong>Classic</strong>
            <small>Traditional single-column serif layout. The familiar resume shape.</small>
            <span class="rb-ats">Single column with standard headings</span>
          </span>
        </label>
        <label class="rb-template">
          <input type="radio" name="rb-template" value="modern" />
          <span>
            <strong>Modern</strong>
            <small>Single-column sans-serif layout with clear hierarchy and standard section headings.</small>
            <span class="rb-ats">Single column; parsing varies by system</span>
          </span>
        </label>
        <label class="rb-template">
          <input type="radio" name="rb-template" value="compact" />
          <span>
            <strong>Compact</strong>
            <small>Readable single-column layout with tighter spacing; may flow onto extra pages.</small>
            <span class="rb-ats">Single column with standard headings</span>
          </span>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <button id="rb-download" class="btn" type="button">Download PDF</button>
        <button id="rb-example" class="btn btn-secondary" type="button">Load example</button>
        <button id="rb-export-json" class="btn btn-secondary" type="button">Export JSON</button>
        <button id="rb-import-json" class="btn btn-secondary" type="button">Import JSON</button>
        <input type="file" id="rb-import-json-file" accept="application/json,.json" hidden />
        <button id="rb-clear" class="btn btn-secondary" type="button">Clear</button>
        <button id="rb-import-again" class="btn btn-secondary" type="button" hidden>Import a resume</button>
      </div>
      <p class="autosave-note"><Icon name="check" size={14} /> Your resume is saved automatically in this browser only.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="rb-error" class="error-box no-print" hidden>    </div>
    <aside id="rb-writing-review" class="rb-writing-review no-print" aria-label="Resume writing review"></aside>
    <div class="tab-bar tab-mobile no-print" role="tablist" aria-label="Editor or preview">
      <button type="button" id="rb-tab-edit" class="tab-btn tab-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true">Edit</button>
      <button type="button" id="rb-tab-preview" class="tab-btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Preview</button>
    </div>
    <div id="rb-workspace" class="resume-workspace">
      <div id="rb-editor" class="resume-editor no-print" aria-label="Resume editor"></div>
      <div class="resume-preview-pane">
        <div id="rb-preview" class="resume-doc resume-classic" aria-label="Resume preview"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <style>
    #rb-import-fields { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin: 0.8rem 0; }
    .rb-review-section h4 { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; font-size: 0.94rem; }
    .rb-review-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.65rem 0.8rem; }
    .rb-review-field { display: grid; gap: 0.25rem; margin: 0; font-size: 0.76rem; font-weight: 650; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
    .rb-review-field input, .rb-review-field textarea { box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; font: 400 0.95rem/1.45 var(--font-sans, sans-serif); letter-spacing: normal; text-transform: none; color: var(--ink); }
    .rb-review-check { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; }
    .rb-review-check input { width: auto; }
    .rb-review-entry { min-width: 0; margin: 0 0 0.7rem; padding: 0.8rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); }
    .rb-review-entry legend { padding: 0 0.3rem; font-weight: 650; }
    #rb-import-status { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0.8rem 0 0; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; }
    #rb-import-status[hidden] { display: none; }
    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      .rb-review-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
  </style>
  <script>
    import { initResumeBuilder } from '../tools/resume-builder';
    import { initResumeImport } from '../tools/resume-import-ui';
    // Each init is independent: a failure in one must never break the other.
    try {
      initResumeBuilder();
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('Resume builder failed to start:', err);
    }
    try {
      initResumeImport();
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('Resume import failed to start:', err);
    }
  </script>
</ToolPage>
